{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Rice Cookout", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I've Been Thinking", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about an unspecified time in the past that is related to now or continues up to now. When you use the Present Perfect tense, the time when the action happened is not important.</p><p>When you use the Present Perfect Continuous tense, the time when the action happened is also not important.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about:<ul><li>experience up to the present</li><li>change that has happened over time</li> <li>an event or action that happened in the past that is important now</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect Continuous:<ul><li>to emphasize that action has continued without stopping until now and may still be taking place</li><li>when we can see the result of an action that happened in the recent past, now</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the Present Perfect tense and the Present Perfect Continuous tense, you often use phrases or clauses for duration. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These phrases or clauses begin with <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in</span> or <span class=\"italic\">since</span>. They answer the question \u201cHow long ... ?\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">since</span> to begin a phrase or a clause (as a connector or as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">for</span> and <span class=\"italic\">in</span> to begin a phrase (as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>Have you talked with the designer in the past few days?</p><p>She's never made me feel bad about not knowing the technical stuff.</p><p>Have you had many hits?</p><p>Yes, I've had quite a few since I started posting.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>I've been working on setting up my website in the evenings.</p><p>The web designer has been making my work easy since we started!</p><p>The blogs have been flying out for a while now!</p><p>You've been sorting through them, right?</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Saying When You are Not Sure About an Issue", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you respond to an opinion, you don't always agree.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you disagree with an opinion it is still important to use a polite response.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at these phrases and sentences:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm not sure ... <br/>Don't you think that could ... <br/>Correct me if I'm wrong, but ... <br/>I'm not sure I agree with you. <br/> I don't agree with you. <br/>That's not entirely true. <br/>Yes, but don't you think ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm not sure I want more writing.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Don't you think that could be bad if it went wrong?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Correct me if I'm wrong, but they could be terrible!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm not sure I agree with you about that.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "never", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not at any time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's never made me feel bad.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a website.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "technical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "methods or skills for a particular activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't know much about the technical stuff to create a website.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something you say or write", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What should I do about the comments the readers leave?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a visit to a website", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Have you had many hits on your blog?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stuff", "type": "name"}, {"content": "things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is all that stuff on the table yours?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to post", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put on a website", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to post these pictures on my website.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sort through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at and divide", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have to sort through the comments before I answer any of them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engen